    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate focused on exploiting soft matchups against mid-rotation arms to claw back ground in our categories. Our most potent play today is **Corbin Carroll** (81.24), who draws a favorable matchup against Bryce Elder. With an optimized lineup slot at #2 and the significant boost from Elder\u2019s 4.40 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** is primed for a high-volume scoring day; his ability to capitalize on the weak SP skill makes him our clear anchor. Close behind him, **Max Muncy** (71.26) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.18) provide high-floor upside against Cody Bradford. Despite Bradford\u2019s lefty status, the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and his elevated 5.29 xERA creates a perfect storm for both **Max Muncy** and **Tyler Soderstrom** to thrive in their respective slots.\n\nWe continue to prioritize speed and situational efficiency, even when facing elite arms. **Brice Turang** (48.04) remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against Tarik Skubal; the optimizer identifies Skubal\u2019s slow delivery as a critical edge, providing a 4% boost to **Brice Turang**'s stolen base projection, which is non-negotiable for our build. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (62.71) offers a strong play against Blade Tidwell, where his 14% dynamic platoon edge more than offsets the slight negative pressure from the catcher\u2019s arm. The closest bench decision today involved **Cole Young** (45.47), who ultimately missed the cut due to **Travis Bazzana** (45.59) maintaining a slightly superior platoon leverage against Casey Mize. We remain on high alert regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Jose Caballero**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Austin Riley**; any unexpected lineup shuffles that drop these players into the bottom third of the order will trigger an immediate downward revision in their efficiency scores. While we await the official cards, we continue to carry the injured **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** on the pine, keeping an eye on our deeper depth chart including **Trevor Story**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot-start needs.",
